🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- a `smol` (short) scalar struct field is sized
🚽 and aligned as 2 bytes, and reads/writes correctly. `yap c` (1, align
🚽 1) at offset 0, `smol s` (2, align 2) at offset 2, `rizz i` (4, align
🚽 4) at offset 4 -> total 8. Short is 2 bytes on both LP64 and wasm32,
🚽 so no per-platform override is needed.
gang Mixed {
    yap c;
    smol s;
    rizz i;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Mixed m;
    m.c = 1;
    m.s = 300;
    m.i = 5;
    yapping("%lu %d %d %d", maxxing(m), m.c, m.s, m.i);
}
